Implemented all seven findings with regression tests:

1. Missing start time: signal-0 `ESRCH` now triggers `exited` and cleanup. Test: “reports exited and cleans up a dead background child without a recorded start time”.
2. Runtime I/O failure: sends `unavailable` with detail. Test: “reports unavailable on a non-terminal registry rewrite failure”.
3. Sweep: removes only the recorded socket and matching key; preserves regular files and unrelated endpoints. Test: “sweeps a recorded socket in directory A without touching directory B”.
4. Work queue: coalesces scans and identity probes. Test: “coalesces stream scans and identity probes while real socket work is pending”.
5. Callbacks: caps active/queued attempts at 8/32, logs dropped refusals, replaces queued re-subscriptions, and preserves notices. Tests include “bounds refusal callbacks to eight active and 32 queued attempts” and “replaces queued terminal re-subscriptions to one address”.
6. Deadline: forwards the environment setting. Test: “forwards the first-line deadline through startBackgroundRun”.
7. Poll: checks regular-file type and 64 KiB cap. Tests: “poll rejects unsafe peer metadata: fifo”, “symlink”, and “oversized”.

